{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_38","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba /Users/smkzw/.codex/memories/MEMORY.md | sed -n '592,610p'\nnl -ba src/ci_workflow/cli.py | sed -n '580,592p'\"","aggregated_output":"   592\t\n   593\t- when designing structured report output, the user rejected CSV/XLSX download-oriented tables: use HTML pages with adapted charts and complete tables hidden by default and expandable on click; preserve three independently designed A/B/C portals while sharing fonts, accessibility, responsiveness, and source conventions. [Task 1] [skysight memory]\n   594\t- when no/insufficient data is found, the user required a third-party-style diagnostic for missed search terms, search-rule errors, or network/data retrieval issues before using a brief explanation or omitting a field; do not fill pages with large empty fields. [Task 1] [skysight memory]\n   595\t- when B-class trials differ in wording, endpoints, or populations, use fuzzy/LLM-assisted substantial-similarity matching and lightly annotate small timepoint differences instead of forcing every variation into a separate display. [Task 1] [skysight memory]\n   596\t- when cross-trial comparison is requested, the user requires clinical semantics rather than exact strings or numerically close values: unknown is not the same, and a hard conflict cannot be overridden by a model. The real HTML must use the same scientific view; an internal helper passing while the portal uses the old glossary is not completion. [Task 2]\n   597\t- for all visible text, labels, and states, the user requires native Chinese clinical-trial language and acceptance from a “懒惰、视觉敏感、非技术背景的资深临床试验医学人员” perspective: inspect real interaction, hierarchy, complete tables, source drawers, and responsive behavior. [Task 2]\n   598\t- when the user says an optional Yaozh route must not block core research or retain credentials/Cookies/profile -> keep it nonblocking, minimally receipted, and distinguish a