ble complete-link buckets to prevent transitive merging; unknown/uncovered observations remain descriptive and are not dropped. A complete clinical unit includes disease/severity, background therapy, population, endpoint/event definition, scale/direction, estimand, denominator, analysis set, statistical form, and actual time window. [Task 2]\n   607\t- P3 uses a complete observation pool to form stable `scientific_group_id`, then projects physical pages after checking row ID, domain, and fact summary. Build `within_trial_longitudinal` before rendering to retain same-trial multi-timepoint identity; reject same-`row_id` cross-domain/fact-summary conflicts and unsupported cross-domain positive proposals. [Task 2]\n   608\t- The current recovery boundary is `context/PAUSE_HANDOFF_20260908_093147.md` at HEAD `bb27ec9d750cf02fb64da5dfe665b2f4b262922d`. Reopen the English implementation directory, hash/current Git state, P3 counterexamples, then independent review, gate, integration, and browser regression in that order. [Task 2]\n   609\t- A Yaozh observation/receipt is only a governed host declaration and secondary cross-check, never direct support for a key clinical conclusion. Require a consumer, freshness decision, executable Yaozh→fact→GateSpec lineage validation, corrupted-record handling, and a real logged-in host smoke before RC. [Task 3]\n   610\t\n   580\t    for records, buckets in pools:\n   581\t        pairs.extend(\n   582\t            build_semantic_review_task(\n   583\t                verification.contract.project_id, records, buckets=buckets,\n   584\t            ).pairs,\n   585\t        )\n   586\t    task = SemanticReviewTask(\n   587\t        task_id=f\"semantic-review-{len(pairs)}\",\n   588\t        project_id=verification.contract.project_id,\n   589\t        policy_version=pairs[0].row_digests[0][:8] if pairs else \"empty\",\n   590\t        pairs=tuple(pairs),\n   591\t    )\n   592\t\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
